                        "entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "present"
                        ],
                        "form": "ободря́я"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "696625f4-e047-4a2a-a212-2f32dd4b0f51",
                        "entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "ободря́в"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "9059503c-e0af-4dfc-9246-311a6c15d446",
                        "entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "tags": [
                            "adverbial",
                            "participle",
                            "past"
                        ],
                        "form": "ободря́вши"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "5acd4582-0319-4878-81ce-213ca473a038",
                        "entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "tags": [
                            "future"
                        ],
                        "form": "буду/будешь… ободря́ть"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                        "entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "glosses": [
                            "внушать бодрость, бодрое настроение; поощрять"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b7a412a-9050-43bd-97d5-77e785fd13c0",
                                "sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                                "text": "Иногда он приходил в отчаяние; графиня ободряла его тогда улыбкой."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "02831d55-8cb4-4e79-885f-b6828778c911",
                                "sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                                "text": "Она боялась ласкать Базарова, и он не ободрял её, не вызывал её на ласки; притом же и Василий Иванович присоветовал ей не очень его «беспокоить»."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "2b8a3081-dc49-457e-9b6e-dedd4990ac14",
                                "sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                                "text": "У всякого малодушного человека, не совсем уверенного в успехе своего дела, является мучительная потребность разуверять себя, ободрять себя, успокоивать."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "77b49617-f6e0-41ad-8120-f183ea7287d4",
                        "source_entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                        "target_lang_word": "cherish",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "cherish",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "430ae01d-11fd-3ecc-abef-dd992be793c8",
                                        "entry_id": "059c4d5b-be18-3f5b-858d-36cef4799f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To treat with affection, care, and tenderness; to nurture or protect with care."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "45f3fea1-734f-427a-828b-b2a026749ac7",
                                                "sense_id": "430ae01d-11fd-3ecc-abef-dd992be793c8",
                                                "text": "[T]he ſame Sun which only cheriſheth and gently warmes his Countrey men, halfe parboyle and tanne other people, and thoſe rayes which ſcorch the aduſted foyles of Calabria and Spaine, only varniſh and guild the green hony-ſuckled plaines and hillocks of England; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "570ef403-44aa-4b6b-89aa-498ec212603d",
                                                "sense_id": "430ae01d-11fd-3ecc-abef-dd992be793c8",
                                                "text": "But the parent, we will ſuppose, cheriſhes his child with an affectionate indulgent care, and with all the circumſpection and aſſiduity that nature requires, in his infirm helpleſs ſtate of infancy; aſſiſts and cheriſhes his underſtanding, in its tender growth does; his utmoſt, according to his ability, to inculcate and impreſs religious principles, […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2eeefa0a-f82a-463e-9f6a-371e0eb90348",
                                                "sense_id": "430ae01d-11fd-3ecc-abef-dd992be793c8",
                                                "text": "On the evening previous to her being brought to my home, my mother had said playfully,—\"I have a pretty present for my Victor—to-morrow he shall have it.\" And when, on the morrow, she presented Elizabeth to me as her promised gift, I, with childish seriousness, interpreted her words literally, and looked upon Elizabeth as mine—mine to protect, love, and cherish."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2141b45c-6208-4645-b9a9-b03ad4be2c86",
                                                "sense_id": "430ae01d-11fd-3ecc-abef-dd992be793c8",
                                                "text": "There were many wooden chairs for the bulk of his visitors, and two wicker arm-chairs with red cloth cushions for superior people. From the packing-cases had emerged some Indian clubs, boxing-gloves, a model oar, and other modest trophies or mementos of his college boating club; and all these articles, together with small knicknacks dating from Oxford days, made a scattered and untidy decoration that Mrs. Clough assiduously dusted and greatly cherished."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                        "entry_id": "059c4d5b-be18-3f5b-858d-36cef4799f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To have a deep appreciation of; to hold dear."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6a66d20c-e546-4a31-8726-4a44524a82c1",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "I cherish your friendship."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2bfeedbd-5a42-4a95-805e-2dea01e5a50a",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "his long-cherished dream"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1663f4e-97ec-46c6-bf46-6ab7e3b2adbd",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "Tuc[ca]. […] Can thy Author doe it impudently enough? / Hiſt[rio]. O, I warrant you, Captaine: and ſpitefully inough too; he ha's one of the moſt ouerflowing villanous wits, in Rome. He will ſlander any man that breathes; If he diſguſt him. / Tucca. I'le know the poor, egregious, nitty Raſcall; and he haue ſuch commendable Qualities, I'le cheriſh him: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ec6d8263-8e35-4f82-a1fe-5b207ce97eac",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "So by cheriſhing Humility, Pride is weakned, by cheriſhing Patience, Violent Paſſions, and Anger, and Peeviſhneſs are deſtroyed, by cheriſhing Purity, and Chaſtity of Heart and Thoughts, Uncleanneſs is mortified, and ſo by cheriſhing heavenly mindedneſs, the love of the world is abated and weakned: and the like might be ſhewed in other inſtances."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "42fdc915-a5fb-4926-9f18-d8d0bf176d13",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "The age in which all thought that trades must be established by bounties and prohibitions; that manufacturers needed their materials and qualities and prices to be prescribed; and that the value of money could be determined by law; was an age which unavoidably cherished the notions that a child's mind could be made to order; that its powers were to be imparted by the schoolmaster; that it was a receptacle into which knowledge was to be put and there built up after its teacher's ideal."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "539f9329-450e-4393-94c7-2ffe04a702a0",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "We came under the influence of his [Mahadev Govind Ranade's] work and his thoughts, and we owe it to ourselves to show that his memory is to us a most cherished possession."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c127076-530a-47ed-b966-aa3798eaa51f",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "We should cherish the life we live / Cherish the love, cherish the life, cherish the love / Cherish the love we have / For as long as we both shall live"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c5f6ed7-5cde-4d11-9bb8-cd51c1fabd4f",
                                                "sense_id": "dad8b503-3746-3fdb-aca6-202394efe88e",
                                                "text": "The Master said: \"The gentleman cherishes virtue; the small man cherishes land. The gentleman cherishes institutions; the small man cherishes favors.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "992b1930-7bdf-38c4-a8f1-597984273909",
                                        "entry_id": "059c4d5b-be18-3f5b-858d-36cef4799f44",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To cheer, to gladden."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2f1cdd3-b902-4f25-bd84-24518c561b7c",
                                                "sense_id": "992b1930-7bdf-38c4-a8f1-597984273909",
                                                "text": "And by the way, as was her wonted guize, / Her merry fitt ſhee freſhly gan to reare, / And did of ioy and iollitie deuize, / Her ſelfe to cheriſh, and her gueſt to cheare: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d593ed68-912b-4099-aa1c-cb4f5133c96f",
                                                "sense_id": "992b1930-7bdf-38c4-a8f1-597984273909",
                                                "text": "The webbe of our life, is of a mingled yarne, good / and ill together: our vertues would bee proud, if our faults / whipt them not, and our crimes would diſpaire if they / were not cheriſh'd by our vertues."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a6315b1-a9af-4f57-a579-03d110dc1d5b",
                        "source_entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                        "target_lang_word": "encourager",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "encourager",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8b639713-f3c7-32f8-83e0-f5a10d1b861e",
                                        "entry_id": "efcec556-2ca4-3ff3-a802-0c881492a8f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inciter à avoir du courage."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1fe2c41f-68b4-4190-95b2-98c972cd5643",
                                                "sense_id": "8b639713-f3c7-32f8-83e0-f5a10d1b861e",
                                                "text": "Les chanteurs sont supérieurs à ceux du même ordre entendus à Paris. La salle, bondée, les encourage par des ovations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d11afae-160e-40d2-8a43-8bf6e9f393da",
                                                "sense_id": "8b639713-f3c7-32f8-83e0-f5a10d1b861e",
                                                "text": "Il m’a encouragé pour les exams, initié au cinéma, m’a abonné au Monde, offert une deuch pour mes vingt et un ans."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "029692e4-4cac-37c7-970d-dd827e04c35e",
                                        "entry_id": "efcec556-2ca4-3ff3-a802-0c881492a8f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Favoriser le progrès, le développement d’une affaire en parlant du commerce, de l’industrie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1d164556-0d8b-4464-aa67-53fa200d8b82",
                                                "sense_id": "029692e4-4cac-37c7-970d-dd827e04c35e",
                                                "text": "Les Abbassides encouragèrent plus encore une civilisation cosmopolite, dont Bagdad fut le centre et l'arabe la linga franca."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "706c7740-a3b5-4485-9703-985efae80b77",
                                                "sense_id": "029692e4-4cac-37c7-970d-dd827e04c35e",
                                                "text": "Encourager la culture du lin, du tabac. — Encourager les sciences, les arts."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ed8a62f-8938-3caa-bb90-05a1926bd4e3",
                                        "entry_id": "efcec556-2ca4-3ff3-a802-0c881492a8f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inciter quelqu’un à faire pour le mieux"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e3712580-909b-4572-9bd6-e1ff41fdb2b1",
                                                "sense_id": "5ed8a62f-8938-3caa-bb90-05a1926bd4e3",
                                                "text": "Encourager la vertu, le talent, le mérite, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "36f94bcc-17ff-345a-9eda-8dabff0b2f6c",
                                        "entry_id": "efcec556-2ca4-3ff3-a802-0c881492a8f5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Exciter quelqu'un, le pousser, le provoquer à ce qu'il a déjà en disposition."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "819760ce-b7cb-41d6-85b1-3c303fd62eb5",
                                                "sense_id": "36f94bcc-17ff-345a-9eda-8dabff0b2f6c",
                                                "text": "Depuis le mois de janvier, en effet, la bonne société de Lausanne se pressait dans les salons du poëte, qu'elle encourageait et récompensait par ses bravos, […]."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "788f614d-83df-4409-9324-19dc6e10da01",
                                                "sense_id": "36f94bcc-17ff-345a-9eda-8dabff0b2f6c",
                                                "text": "Encourager le vice, le crime, la révolte, etc.,"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "3b64de8f-8e2a-4744-bfd6-a3cecda8e361",
                        "source_entry_id": "0511e0c8-330c-328f-bed6-2565397feef4",
                        "source_sense_id": "a8241602-8fde-352f-82d9-353cb0708c37",
                        "target_lang_word": "réconforter",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "réconforter",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0f0415a-070b-38c0-bbc1-8e1ad1d0d478",
                                        "entry_id": "bbcd45d5-314f-379f-b219-39e7cb536029",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Relever les forces, ranimer, remonter, tant au sens physique ou médical, qu'au sens moral."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8ddedafe-3106-4e12-92ce-af969bdb2bce",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f0415a-070b-38c0-bbc1-8e1ad1d0d478",
                                                "text": "Platon, le divin Platon, n'était en verve que lorsqu'il était en pointe de vin. Ennius ne travaillait jamais à son poème héroïque, que Bacchus ne l’eût réconforté, et Alcée n'écrivait ses tragédies que lorsqu'il était ivre."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d8632e0b-d13f-471d-8aa6-67dd24e52edd",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f0415a-070b-38c0-bbc1-8e1ad1d0d478",
                                                "text": "Vos bonnes paroles m’ont réconforté à l’heure du découragement."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8de9ec41-7f06-4be6-9174-2390227bee9c",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f0415a-070b-38c0-bbc1-8e1ad1d0d478",
                                                "text": "Il fut longtemps à se réconforter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "36f6e366-16eb-48db-94f3-a6ba5db07d0f",
                                                "sense_id": "f0f0415a-070b-38c0-bbc1-8e1ad1d0d478",
                                                "text": "L’amitié réconforte."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "7dbdfe37-ff26-3d7c-b90f-51e45f349c7e",
                                        "entry_id": "bbcd45d5-314f-379f-b219-39e7cb536029",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Consoler dans l’affliction."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "51c67fd9-81f6-4bf7-9680-0b9cfda170f4",
                                                "sense_id": "7dbdfe37-ff26-3d7c-b90f-51e45f349c7e",
                                                "text": "Toujours penchée sur le grabat des âmes, Elle lavait les plaies, pansait les blessures, réconfortait les défaillantes langueurs des conversions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3f46a64-1248-4827-a2b2-8ac4389670e7",
                                                "sense_id": "7dbdfe37-ff26-3d7c-b90f-51e45f349c7e",
                                                "text": "Elle restait là où elle était, immobile, inconsolable et comme une chiffe aux mains des bonnes femmes qui s'efforçaient de la réconforter."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "25f79c50-172e-4a5d-95bc-f3a9ef8148bc",
                                                "sense_id": "7dbdfe37-ff26-3d7c-b90f-51e45f349c7e",
                                                "text": "Voilà qui va réconforter les mourants, car la délégation au grand complet visite maintenant les deux salles où sont entassés les cholériques."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
